# FCSpreadSheetPlus — Project file

## Description
A FreeCAD spreadsheet workbench (Python addon) similar to the default
FreeCAD Spreadsheet workbench. It reuses FreeCAD's built-in
`Spreadsheet::Sheet` objects through a thin Python wrapper and exposes a
custom workbench with toolbar/menu commands.

## Tech stack
- FreeCAD 1.x / 2.x (AppImages at `~/Applications/`)
- Python 3.11 (bundled with FreeCAD)
- Namespace workbench structure: `freecad/fcspreadsheetplus/`
- Addon Manager metadata via `package.xml`

## Architecture
- `freecad/fcspreadsheetplus/__init__.py` — headless entry (exports `__version__`)
- `freecad/fcspreadsheetplus/version.py` — `__version__`
- `freecad/fcspreadsheetplus/init_gui.py` — GUI entry: registers icons, translations, commands, workbench
- `freecad/fcspreadsheetplus/workbench.py` — `FCSpreadSheetPlusWorkbench` (Gui.Workbench)
- `freecad/fcspreadsheetplus/commands/` — command classes (toolbar/menu actions): CreateSheet, CreateMasterSheet, CreateConfigRef, EditConfigTable, SwitchConfiguration
- `freecad/fcspreadsheetplus/dialogs/` — `TableEditorDialog` (table editor)
- `freecad/fcspreadsheetplus/view_providers.py` — `ConfigRefViewProvider` (tree icon)
- `freecad/fcspreadsheetplus/sheet.py` — `Sheet` wrapper around `Spreadsheet::Sheet`
- `freecad/fcspreadsheetplus/table.py` — configuration table model (rows = configs, cols = params)
- `freecad/fcspreadsheetplus/master_sheet.py` — `MasterSheet` wrapper + `create()`
- `freecad/fcspreadsheetplus/config_ref.py` — `ConfigRef` FeaturePython (row selection, cross-file link)
- `freecad/fcspreadsheetplus/resources/` — icons + translations + `Resources` manager

## Install / dev loop
- Dev (no install): `~/Applications/FreeCAD_1.1.3-Linux-x86_64-py311.AppImage -M ~/projects/FCSpreadSheetPlus`
- Or symlink: `ln -s ~/projects/FCSpreadSheetPlus ~/.local/share/FreeCAD/Mod/FCSpreadSheetPlus`
- Headless tests: extract AppImage once, then
  `./squashfs-root/AppRun freecadcmd -M ~/projects/FCSpreadSheetPlus tests/test_sheet.py`

## Notes / decisions
- License: LGPL-2.1-or-later (same as FreeCAD)
- Maintainer: Chris (email placeholder)
- ConfigRef parameters are read-only (read-through model): two-way editing is
  deliberately rejected so a naive edit can't silently change other parts that
  share the same configuration cell. Revisit only on user feedback.
- Cell read API: use `Sheet.getContents(address)` for raw cell content;
  `Sheet.get(address)` only returns cells exposed as properties, so the
  `Sheet` wrapper routes `get()` through `getContents()`.

## Plan
The detailed technical plan lives in `PLAN.md`. Core idea: a single **MasterSheet**
per project (reusable across files), and a per-part **ConfigRef** that links to it
and selects a named row, so many parts share one spreadsheet without copying it.

## Docs (written as we go)
- `docs/usage.md` — how-to: table layout, scripting quick start, cross-file, value types.
- `docs/api.md` — reference for `Table`, `MasterSheet`, `ConfigRef`, `Sheet`.
- Convention: each phase ships its docs in the same commit.

