## FreeCAD gotchas (verified)
- FreeCADCmd executes scripts with `__name__` set to the script basename (NOT
  `"__main__"`) — test scripts must call `main()` unconditionally.
- `sys.exit(n)` inside FreeCADCmd propagates the exit code, but Python stdout is
  not auto-flushed — use `print(..., flush=True)` or prints get lost.
- Run scripts with `freecadcmd -M <repo> script.py`, not the bare AppImage
  `python` (which cannot `import FreeCAD`).
- `Sheet.getContents(addr)` returns **string cells with a leading `'` marker**
  (numbers are returned bare). Strip it when reading text.
- `Sheet.set(addr, value)` requires a str; numeric-looking strings become
  numbers, anything else becomes a string.
- `Sheet.removeRows("3", 1)` / `removeColumns("B", 1)` take a 1-based row string
  and a column letter respectively.
- `App::PropertyXLink` links to objects in other documents. Setting it to an
  external object requires the **owner document to be saved first**, otherwise
  it throws "Owner document not saved" (FreeCAD needs the path to compute the
  relative link).
- Do NOT add/remove dynamic properties in a FeaturePython `onChanged` — it fires
  during document restore when external link targets aren't loaded yet, which
  corrupts the exposed properties. Do it in `execute()` (runs on recompute).
- A dynamic property name must not collide with a document object's Python
  attributes (methods like `recompute`) or the FeaturePython `Proxy` property.
  Guard with `hasattr(obj, name)` before `addProperty`, and only sync the
  `ManagedParameters` list in `_sync_values` — never the full parameter list —
  so colliding names are skipped instead of crashing on `getTypeIdOfProperty`.
